  ./stats/com.oracle.database.jdbc/ojdbc-provider-azure/1.1.0/forge-publication.json:61:    "review_comment": "Approved after reviewing the single-coordinate diff, test sources, build configuration, metadata file scope, index and resolved statistics. The tests use public APIs from a separate package, are not scaffold-only or version-pinned, do not skip or tolerate Native Image failures, and contain no forbidden compatibility override or runtime-class-definition behavior. The narrowly scoped Azure Core config exclusion addresses a transitive dependency's unconditional native-image.properties initialization, rather than test-specific behavior. Dynamic-access evidence is a valid 0/0 case, so no percentage or entry-count mismatch gate applies. Local gate evidence was green, and the Forge-owned finalization completed all three native lanes, metadata/style/generated-test checks, and statistics generation without changing the publishable tree.",
  ./stats/com.nimbusds/nimbus-jose-jwt/4.0/forge-publication.json:59:    "finding_body": "The new 4.0 test project copied `--enable-url-protocols=https` into `build.gradle` without satisfying the native-flag necessity rule. The adapted 4.0 tests use `URI` values and perform no HTTPS URL access, so the flag was not required by the library or a transitive dependency. All three Native Image lanes passed after its removal.",
